//============================================================================================================================================
//                                                            SLATEUI.SYMBOLINDEX
//============================================================================================================================================
// 🧩 Symbol roll for SlateUI — Every primitive control as one immediate-mode free function over a rectangle — no widget owns anything, and the theme arrives by reference.

%format   symbolindex 1.0
%scope    layer
%path     Engine/SlateUI
%folders  16
%symbols  463

//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//                                                     FOLDER INDEXES
//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

I Api    | Api/Api.symbolindex       | 34 sym  | Every primitive control as one immediate-mode free function over a rectangle — no widget owns anything, and the theme arrives by reference.
I Source | Source/Source.symbolindex | 91 sym  | The four choosing controls — a crossing nub, a run of exclusive pills, a dropped list, and a row of independent switches.
I Api    | Api/Api.symbolindex       | 8 sym   | The register made visible — reports grouped by their declared class, measures presented at their producer's tier.
I Source | Source/Source.symbolindex | 10 sym  | Seven declared classes presented at three weights, and the measures beneath them — nothing inferred, nothing held.
I Api    | Api/Api.symbolindex       | 22 sym  | Vector glyphs rasterised once and keyed by content — two names sharing bytes share one texture, and no vendor identity escapes.
I Source | Source/Source.symbolindex | 24 sym  | Drives the vector rasteriser and the staging transfer — the one file in which a glyph becomes a vendor texture identity.
I Api    | Api/Api.symbolindex       | 10 sym  | The one seam the interface library crosses — device handles in, recorded commands out, no ImGui spelling.
I Source | Source/Source.symbolindex | 9 sym   | The only translation unit in the engine that includes ImGui.
I Api    | Api/Api.symbolindex       | 10 sym  | Presents RowSequence through RankIndex and writes intent back — holding no relation of its own.
I Source | Source/Source.symbolindex | 15 sym  | The counted span presented, and every gesture over it turned into a declared intent.
I Api    | Api/Api.symbolindex       | 7 sym   | The transaction sequence made visible and scrubbable — every row read from `RevisionSequence`, nothing held here.
I Source | Source/Source.symbolindex | 19 sym  | `Inspector.tsx`'s revision timeline over the real sequence — bubble column, spine, card, fold.
I Api    | Api/Api.symbolindex       | 10 sym  | The one palette and the one set of layout extents every panel reads — resolved once a tick, held by nobody else.
I Source | Source/Source.symbolindex | 10 sym  | The one translation unit in which an interface colour literal and a layout extent literal are permitted.
I Api    | Api/Api.symbolindex       | 75 sym  | The slot ledger a workspace fills at activation and the desk walks each tick — the host names no concrete panel.
I Source | Source/Source.symbolindex | 109 sym | Declaration, release and resolution over a fixed panel ledger — no allocation, no ImGui, no vendor spelling.

//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//                                                        SYMBOLS
//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

T ControlInteraction                    | Api/ControlPanel.h              | 30-37     | What one control did this tick — the pointer over it, and the three points of an edit's lifecycle. on every `EditDeclared`, and seals on `EditSealed`. A control that reported only "the reading changed" would leave the caller unable to tell a drag from a run of separate edits, and the defect presents as a revision row per pixel of pointer travel — which is exactly `84`'s merge requirement failing. `EditDeclared` may be false on that tick; sealing is not conditional on it.
E ControlStroke                         | Api/ControlPanel.h              | 47-65     | The chrome glyphs a control paints from line and arc primitives when no uploaded glyph is named. rasteriser. A panel that wants authored art names a depot slot instead and the stroke is not consulted.
T ControlRowSplit                       | Api/ControlPanel.h              | 73-77     | One control row divided into its label column and the field beside it.
F ResolveControlRow                     | Api/ControlPanel.h              | 88        | Divides one row into remix's 88 px label column and the field that takes the remainder. falls back to `LabelColumnRatio`. Frontier clipped the field to nothing instead, and the defect presents as a docked-narrow panel whose sliders are all zero pixels wide and cannot be grabbed at all.
F PresentControlLabel                   | Api/ControlPanel.h              | 93        | Paints one row's caption in the muted text colour, clipped to its column.
F PresentControlStroke                  | Api/ControlPanel.h              | 99        | Paints one stroke centred in a square, at the coverage and thickness the caller declares.
E TextPlacement                         | Api/ControlPanel.h              | 115-120   | Where a text run sits inside the rectangle it was given.
F PresentSurfaceFill                    | Api/ControlPanel.h              | 127       | Fills one rectangle at the declared corner radius. `999px` for exactly that and refusing it would make every pill site carry its own arithmetic.
F PresentSurfaceOutline                 | Api/ControlPanel.h              | 132       | Outlines one rectangle at the declared corner radius and thickness.
F PresentTextRun                        | Api/ControlPanel.h              | 141       | Prints one run of text placed inside a rectangle, clipped to it.
F DeclareClip                           | Api/ControlPanel.h              | 153       | Narrows the recording to one rectangle until the matching reclaim. leaves the whole rest of the tick clipped to a panel's interior, and the defect presents as the tab strip vanishing rather than as anything the panel did.
F ReclaimClip                           | Api/ControlPanel.h              | 158       | Returns the recording to whatever it was clipped to before the matching declaration.
F MeasuredTextExtent                    | Api/ControlPanel.h              | 163       | The horizontal extent one run of text would occupy at the declared scale.
F AdvanceVisibleOffset                  | Api/ControlPanel.h              | 174       | Advances a hand-rolled list's visible offset by the wheel, bounded to what the content leaves. scrolled view snaps back to content rather than presenting an empty band under the last row.
F PresentValueSlider                    | Api/ControlPanel.h              | 197       | A label, a fixed 78 px value box, and a track whose knob sits at the reading's fraction of its span. ExtentExhausted when the field cannot carry the value box and a grabbable track its knob; clamping the span silently instead gives the artist a control that looks live and is not.
F PresentScalarEntry                    | Api/ControlPanel.h              | 214       | An unbounded scalar: the same value box, and a centre-knobbed track that accumulates travel rather than mapping position, so the reading may leave any span. readout — a knob that travelled would imply a span this control does not have.
F PresentVectorEntry                    | Api/ControlPanel.h              | 227       | Three value boxes side by side, each capped with its axis letter, each dragging its own component.
F PresentBooleanEntry                   | Api/ControlPanel.h              | 243       | A 50×32 travel whose nub crosses on a click. holding its own would be retained state — which this file has none of by construction.
F PresentSelectionEntry                 | Api/ControlPanel.h              | 255       | A wrapping run of pills, the chosen one filled with the accent and lettered in the on-accent colour.
T DropdownCarry                         | Api/ControlPanel.h              | 266-272   | What a dropdown carries between ticks — its openness and the anchor its list drops from. open together, which is the defect that follows from a control holding openness of its own.
F PresentDropdown                       | Api/ControlPanel.h              | 281       | A 26 px head with a caret cap, and a hand-rolled list beneath it. tab overlays are not: every trapezoid is already on that recording, and a popup sits beneath it.
F PresentSegmentRow                     | Api/ControlPanel.h              | 294       | A 26 px pill row — the reference's `.seg`, filled when it is on. choice, so each pill carries its own boolean and pressing one does not clear the others.
V ControlTextExtent                     | Api/ControlPanel.h              | 306       | ?
T TextCarry                             | Api/ControlPanel.h              | 312-318   | One open text edit — the edited text, never the committed one. never written during the edit, so an abandoned rename leaves no trace and a refused seal leaves none.
F PresentTextEntry                      | Api/ControlPanel.h              | 324       | A rounded field the artist types into, opened by a click and sealed by Enter or by a press elsewhere.
F PresentInlineTextEditor               | Api/ControlPanel.h              | 335       | A text edit with no field of its own, painted over whatever it is renaming. the trapezoid beneath it stays visible and the artist can see what is being renamed.
F PresentPathEntry                      | Api/ControlPanel.h              | 345       | A path field and the round browse cap beside it. chooser itself would be a panel holding what it presents.
F PresentColourEntry                    | Api/ControlPanel.h              | 362       | A fully rounded bar carrying a swatch disc, the coordinate printed, and a caret cap. never spells a transfer — `14` §5 places the interface after the display projection, and a control that converted here would be the second transfer the whole arrangement exists to prevent.
F PresentMenuPill                       | Api/ControlPanel.h              | 371       | A caption pill that reads as pressable — what a menu band is a run of.
F PresentGlyphButton                    | Api/ControlPanel.h              | 386       | A square glyph that answers a press — the uploaded glyph when a depot slot is named, the stroke otherwise. painting nothing at all — a missing icon that still answers a press is recoverable, an invisible button is not. The stroke is therefore always supplied, even where a slot is expected to resolve. already documents it as an integer whose meaning only its own source knows.
F PresentSectionHeader                  | Api/ControlPanel.h              | 396       | A 29 px accordion header with a twisty that turns a quarter as it opens.
T CarouselCarry                         | Api/ControlPanel.h              | 404-409   | What a carousel carries between ticks — which pane is presented and how far the slide has travelled.
