T StripCarrier                          | Source/WorkspaceStripInternal.h | 51-56     | The rectangle a strip and its body occupy, and which of the two things owns it. no index. Both being absent is a carrier nothing can resolve an intent against.
T DeferredIntent                        | Source/WorkspaceStripInternal.h | 66-98     | Every structural amendment one tick asked for, applied once the whole desk has been traversed. walking. Applying inside the traversal invalidates the very references it is iterating, and the defect presents as a leaf painted at another leaf's rectangle rather than as a crash.
F PresentOccupantStrip                  | Source/WorkspaceStripInternal.h | 109       | Paints one carrier's body and trapezoid strip and resolves every pointer intent the strip carries. which is not structure — it is the record that lets a click activate and only travel tear.
F AdvanceWorkspaceDrag                  | Source/WorkspaceStripInternal.h | 125       | Turns a travelled press into a drag, advances the one in flight, and applies it on release.
F PresentFloatingWindows                | Source/WorkspaceStripInternal.h | 134       | Paints every floating window, topmost last, and resolves the input of the topmost one under the pointer. panels only in leaves would make tearing a tab out of the desk silently discard its panel arrangement.
F LocateWindowCovering                  | Source/WorkspaceStripInternal.h | 141       | The topmost floating window covering a point, or zero.
F PaintDragPreview                      | Source/WorkspaceStripInternal.h | 146       | Washes the resolved landing in the accent, above everything else the tick painted. back out of every band leaves the desk exactly as it was found.
F PresentPanelLayer                     | Source/WorkspaceStripInternal.h | 160       | Presents one body's panel boxes — docked beneath, floating above — and resolves the input each one carries. its own extent would paint at the depth the band carried before the drag rather than the one it carries. recorded over it would sit on top of whatever the workspace draws into the body.
